As in my other work, the economic logic deployed here is overwhelmingly verbal.
 I hope this makes this book accessible to a wider audience.
 This is also the manner in which I “think economically” and thus the manner in which I write.
 I point this out, first, with the aim of retaining non-economist readers, or others more comfortable with nontechnical analyses, who might otherwise set this book aside now in the mistaken belief that a flurry of equations are to follow.
 I point this out, second, so that readers committed to the view that formalism is the only, or the only legitimate, way to say anything useful can set me aside now and return to their mathematical exercises.
